 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The channel starts to conduct between 0.5 V and 1.1 V of gate voltage (0.9 V typ at 10 µA). On-resistance is guaranteed at two drive levels: 21.0 mΩ max at 4.5 V and 6.3 A, 27.0 mΩ max at 2.5 V and 5.1 A. Charging the gate to 4.5 V with 10 V and 6.3 A at the drain takes 8.9 nC typ, of which 4.4 nC is Miller charge; in Fig 6 the plateau sits near 1.6 V. Internal gate resistance is 1.7 Ω typ. The threshold drops as the junction warms (Fig 15). In Fig 13 on-resistance at 2.5 V drive holds near 20 mΩ up to about 15 A and then climbs steeply, reaching 80 mΩ near 30 A; at 4.5 V it rises only from about 16 mΩ to 21 mΩ between 1 A and 50 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate charge waveform",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Under constant gate current, VGS rises to the plateau while QGS goes in, holds flat while QGD goes in, then climbs to the final drive level VG; QG is the total charge (Fig 14a)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "td(on) is measured from VGS at 10 % to VDS at 90 %, tr from VDS at 90 % to 10 %; td(off) from VGS at 90 % to VDS at 10 %, and tf from VDS at 10 % to 90 % (Fig 10b). With VDD = 10 V, 1.0 A, RG = 6.8 Ω and 4.5 V drive they are 4.9, 7.5, 19 and 12 ns typ."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat and current",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Current and power ratings are referred to ambient. Junction-to-ambient resistance is 100 °C/W max mounted on one square inch of copper, and 99 °C/W max for times under 10 s. Dissipation is rated 1.3 W at 25 °C and 0.80 W at 70 °C, derating at 0.01 W/°C. The continuous drain current limit falls from 6.3 A at 25 °C to zero at 150 °C (Fig 9). On-resistance at 4.5 V and 6.3 A rises to about 1.5 times its 25 °C value at 150 °C (Fig 4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Safe operating area",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Fig 8 gives single-pulse limits at 25 °C ambient with the junction at 150 °C, for 100 µs, 1 ms and 10 ms pulses; at low drain voltage the boundary is set by on-resistance."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The integral diode carries 1.3 A continuous and 32 A pulsed, drops at most 1.2 V at 6.3 A, and recovers from 1.3 A at 100 A/µs in 12 ns typ (18 ns max) with 5.1 nC typ (7.7 nC max) of charge."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and marking",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "The Micro3 outline conforms to JEDEC TO-236AB. The top face carries the part code (S for this part), a year digit Y, a work-week letter W and a lot code; a bar over the week letter marks a lead-free part, a bar under the part code marks copper bond wire, and a bar under the year digit marks a halogen-free part. For work weeks 1 to 26 Y is the last digit of the year; for weeks 27 to 52 Y is a letter, A for 2001 or 2011 up to K for 2010 or 2020. W runs A to Z across the 26 weeks of each half year. The scheme applies to parts built after 02/26/2001."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Qualification",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "RoHS compliant and free of lead, bromide and halogen; moisture sensitivity level 1; qualified to the consumer level."
  }
 ],
